.TH COWSAY 1 "FUZIX" "Ripple"
.SH NAME
cowsay \- display a talking cow
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
cowsay [-bdgpstwy] [-W width] [message ...]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print a cow saying the supplied message, or read text from standard input.
-W sets the wrapping width. Eye options include -b, -d, -g, -p, -s, -t,
-w and -y. --help displays usage and --version displays attribution.
.PP
Input is bounded to 4096 characters; wrapping preserves multiple lines.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cowsay Hello Ripple
echo 'Unix is alive' | cowsay
.fi
